MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_001: Why not use the terrain? Retreat and lure them into\nthe valley, then surround their forces and strike.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_002: That'll be tedious with their reinforcements. I say we\njust charge forward and split them apart.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_003: Ahh. Nothing's changed. Even on matters\nof strategy, you and I never see eye to eye.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_004: It's a wonder we've been friends for so long,\nconsidering how much we clash.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_005: Well, we did hate each other at the start.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_006: I was just trying to make conversation with my\nfellow squire.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_007: The commoner with the amazing skills that people\nhad been buzzing about.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_008: Well, I was annoyed to be approached so casually\nby some spoiled noble who'd never known hardship.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_009: And you started the conversation with the nastiest\nremark. I'll never forget it.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_010: "Your name might have gotten you this far, but it's\nnot worth a damn on the battlefield."
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_011: I still remember how red your face got.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_012: Good thing there were people there to hold you back\nwhen you lunged at me. I might have hurt a noble.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_013: You were always provoking me! I thought you were\nan absolute bastard.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_014: And I thought you were an idiot. I was sure you'd\nget yourself killed.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_015: Certainly, I didn't think you'd be promoted. At best\nyou'd end up as one of my pawns.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_016: I can't even count the number of times we've\nargued since then.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_017: At times, I wanted to leave the knighthood, I was so\nfed up with you.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_018: But my loyalty to the kingdom kept me holding on.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_019: Our homeland has been in a sorry state since\nGilchris's reign.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_020: I'm just glad I survived. It would have been a shame\nto die for such a foolish king.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_021: If I died for my loyalty, I would have no regrets.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_C_022: Heh. Yet another thing we don't see eye to eye about.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_001: Leaving it to you, Nathan. Wipe them out!
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_002: You got it. Not one step closer!
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_003: Thank you for having my back. When we're together,\nI feel like I can't lose.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_004: Agreed. No matter how harsh the battle, as a pair,\nwe've always survived.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_005: And triumphed. There's a reason the Aragonian army\ncalled us into action before anyone else.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_006: We were superior to all others, so it was only natural.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_007: Your wisdom has gotten me through so many\ndifficult battles.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_008: Don't be too modest, now. Your bravery has gotten\nme through plenty as well.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_009: Many of my plans wouldn't have been possible\nwithout you.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_010: You do ask me to do some preposterous things.\nEveryone else would say, "Only Nathan can do it."
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_011: But I'm glad I at least have your trust. It makes me\nfeel like I'm at the center of your battle planning.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_012: Who knew war would forge us into such\nstrong friends?
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_013: For my part, I'm tired of being lumped together as\nthe Twin Jewels of Arago.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_014: It almost makes us sound like equals, when I'm\nclearly better than you.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_015: Are you now? I train hard to leave you in my dust.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_016: You must be struggling. If I train hard enough, I can\nput a gap between us in an instant.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_017: I wonder how long we'll keep having this argument.\nThe truth is we're evenly matched.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_018: Maybe it was our destiny to fight side by side,\nkeeping each other alive...
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_019: Must my destiny be with you? I'd prefer to share my\nfuture with a beautiful maiden.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_020: You're always so cruel with your words! You're lucky\nthat, now, they calm me down.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_021: For my part, I'll admit I've come to find your naïveté\nendearing.
MID_SE_Nat_Hri_B_022: I have no intention of losing you. None at all.